<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anarchy at Samarra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/861">861</a>–<a href="/years/870">870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-anarchy">The Anarchy</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarra">Samarra</a> was a period of turmoil in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> from 861 to 870, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> ruled from Samarra. It began with the murder of the caliph al-Mutawakkil by Turkish military officers, after which several caliphs were made and unmade by the army. It demonstrated the dominance of the Turkish soldiery and severely weakened the caliphate's authority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anarchy-at-samarra.jpg" alt="Anarchy at Samarra" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gabagool · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbasids850.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
